This project is informed by two GPL-3.0 engines for the same game:

  G-Engine, by Clark Kromenaker - https://github.com/kromenak/gengine
  GK3Reborn                     - https://github.com/Devion/GK3Reborn

The Barn archive layout in crates/barn follows G-Engine's BarnFile.cpp and
GK3Reborn's docs/formats/barn.md. The LZO1X decoder follows the structure of
the reference lzo1x_decompress_safe algorithm.

Behaviour taken from G-Engine (action case ranking, camera collision,
conversations, title cards) is noted where it is implemented. The tables
the original keeps in code rather than data, and that G-Engine
reconstructed, are taken from it too: the fingerprint kit's objects, the
driving map's places and routes, the binoculars' aim, and SIDNEY's files,
search events, analyses, translations, fake IDs and suspects. So are the
driving map's hints (gk3/src/map.rs), from G-Engine's HintManager, and the
scene functions' mends for faults in the original's files (MS3, CSE). The
rules for when each timeblock ends (crates/game/src/timeblocks.rs), the
score each event is worth (crates/game/src/scores.rs), and the temples'
puzzles (CS2's laser heads, TE1's chessboard, TE3's pendulum, TE5's bridge,
TE6's fight) and the church's angels were read from the original
executable; see docs/re-*.md.

The Bink decoder (crates/bink) and the Cinepak decoder
(crates/media/src/cinepak.rs) are ports of FFmpeg's bink.c, binkaudio.c,
binkdsp.c and cinepak.c (LGPL-2.1-or-later, https://ffmpeg.org), used here
under the GPL as the LGPL allows.

